(1647949, 221338, 17507, '<td valign="top">master librodo?<br/>I will continue my comment based on the assumption that my ID of the photographer is correct-<br/>I''m impressed by a lot of your work, and most of it is well beyond my ability to criticise. But this one doesn''t seem to hold up to your usual standard of excellence.while technically well executed, the model looks disengaged, with a rather bland expression. Your photos often capture an air of grace around your subjects, but that is lacking here. I don''t know if the white stuff is actually milk, but it looks strangely thick. 5 from me</td>', 'master librodo?I will continue my comment based on the assumption that my ID of the photographer is correct-I''m impressed by a lot of your work, and most of it is well beyond my ability to criticise. But this one doesn''t seem to hold up to your usual standard of excellence.while technically well executed, the model looks disengaged, with a rather bland expression. Your photos often capture an air of grace around your subjects, but that is lacking here. I don''t know if the white stuff is actually milk, but it looks strangely thick. 5 from me', '2005-08-26 17:06:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(1647951, 221562, 17507, '<td valign="top">this is such a cool idea! if the composition weren''t so bottom heavy, I''d probably give this an 8 or more--but as it is, it''s a 6</td>', 'this is such a cool idea! if the composition weren''t so bottom heavy, I''d probably give this an 8 or more--but as it is, it''s a 6', '2005-08-26 17:07:18.000000', NULL, 1),
