(1661452, 222091, 3102, '<td valign="top">Absolutely well-deserved!  This is just the kind of shot that should be prominently featured on the front page of the site.  Kudos for another extremely well-executed shot!</td>', 'Absolutely well-deserved!  This is just the kind of shot that should be prominently featured on the front page of the site.  Kudos for another extremely well-executed shot!', '2005-08-31 11:02:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(1661459, 222163, 28710, '<td valign="top">This is really good. I don''t dislike the background too much, but I agree with others who said a bigger saucer would have helped underneath. <br/> <br/>The effect of a hole in milk is really good. I wonder if you could have made the milk look better if you had used cream or something a little heavier instead. There seems to be a lot of weird pink-orange colouring too. This is likely a byproduct of your main light source penetrating too far into the milk.</td>', 'This is really good. I don''t dislike the background too much, but I agree with others who said a bigger saucer would have helped underneath.  The effect of a hole in milk is really good. I wonder if you could have made the milk look better if you had used cream or something a little heavier instead. There seems to be a lot of weird pink-orange colouring too. This is likely a byproduct of your main light source penetrating too far into the milk.', '2005-08-31 11:04:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(1661460, 221081, 35804, '<td valign="top">63? Next time we will do splooshes...or a sploosh on a cow?...or maybe we could drop a cow into a giant vat of milk then throw cookies and fruit at it...talk about the ulimate sploosh! ...nah  : }</td>', '63? Next time we will do splooshes...or a sploosh on a cow?...or maybe we could drop a cow into a giant vat of milk then throw cookies and fruit at it...talk about the ulimate sploosh! ...nah  : }', '2005-08-31 11:04:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(1661464, 221637, 28276, '<td valign="top">some one asked during the challenge how this was set up, so i thought i''d give a quick rundown : <br/> <br/>basically, i set up a bowl of milk on the counter and mounted my d70<br/>and tamron 90mm to the tripod just slightly higher than the bowl.  i<br/>manually focused on my finger at the surface of the water in the<br/>middle of the bowl.<br/>for this shot, the sb-600 flash was set in wireless mode just beside<br/>the bowl to the left of the lens with a lumiquest ultrasoft to give<br/>the soft lighting.  with a turkey baster, i dropped chocolate milk<br/>into the bowl and just kept my finger on the shutter button (taking<br/>about 25+ shots per baster full)<br/>in total, it took more than 150 shots to get this one to turn out.<br/>hurray for digital...<br/>the real difficulty was getting the drops to hit in time w/ the<br/>shutter and flash and to make all the drops hit the exact spot i''d<br/>prefocused on...<br/>because of the kitchen lights and the flash, i never got the white<br/>balance to a point i was happy with, which is why the milk is too blue<br/>and the chocolate milk too orange... oh well.  next time i''ll know<br/>better...</td>', 'some one asked during the challenge how this was set up, so i thought i''d give a quick rundown :  basically, i set up a bowl of milk on the counter and mounted my d70and tamron 90mm to the tripod just slightly higher than the bowl.  imanually focused on my finger at the surface of the water in themiddle of the bowl.for this shot, the sb-600 flash was set in wireless mode just besidethe bowl to the left of the lens with a lumiquest ultrasoft to givethe soft lighting.  with a turkey baster, i dropped chocolate milkinto the bowl and just kept my finger on the shutter button (takingabout 25+ shots per baster full)in total, it took more than 150 shots to get this one to turn out.hurray for digital...the real difficulty was getting the drops to hit in time w/ theshutter and flash and to make all the drops hit the exact spot i''dprefocused on...because of the kitchen lights and the flash, i never got the whitebalance to a point i was happy with, which is why the milk is too blueand the chocolate milk too orange... oh well.  next time i''ll knowbetter...', '2005-08-31 11:06:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(1661473, 220441, 28710, '<td valign="top">Good use of the border, well matched. <br/> <br/>Also, I like the shadows on top of the milk. That is what really made the pic come together.<br/> <br/>Could have done better as a portrait though as others said.<br/> <br/>Nice work!</td>', 'Good use of the border, well matched.  Also, I like the shadows on top of the milk. That is what really made the pic come together. Could have done better as a portrait though as others said. Nice work!', '2005-08-31 11:10:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(1661477, 222091, 28276, '<td valign="top">i had this shot as my second favorite, but called it to win.  (my favorite didn''t do too well.  no accounting for taste, eh?)<br/> <br/>anyway...  well deserved blue.  amazing capture and the fact you got in in about a sixth of the tries it too me to get my splash proves you are the man</td>', 'i had this shot as my second favorite, but called it to win.  (my favorite didn''t do too well.  no accounting for taste, eh?) anyway...  well deserved blue.  amazing capture and the fact you got in in about a sixth of the tries it too me to get my splash proves you are the man', '2005-08-31 11:12:22.000000', NULL, 0),
