(1723609, 221972, 42328, '<td valign="top">What an awesome idea!  (I happen to love old horror movies).  You''ve executed it so well...the shadows on the wall are perfect.  How did you aquire that mixer?  My best friend has a stove in her kitchen from 1951...it''s baby blue and oh so fun.  You''ve just reminded me that I must photograph it.</td>', 'What an awesome idea!  (I happen to love old horror movies).  You''ve executed it so well...the shadows on the wall are perfect.  How did you aquire that mixer?  My best friend has a stove in her kitchen from 1951...it''s baby blue and oh so fun.  You''ve just reminded me that I must photograph it.', '2005-09-20 10:06:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(1724325, 221972, 35804, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Napalm Nymph:</b></div><hr/><i> What an awesome idea!  (I happen to love old horror movies).  You''ve executed it so well...the shadows on the wall are perfect.  How did you aquire that mixer?  My best friend has a stove in her kitchen from 1951...it''s baby blue and oh so fun.  You''ve just reminded me that I must photograph it. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>The mixer was my father-in-laws, he, I think, "liberated" it from a closed down diner in Philly...so the story goes. I just LOVE fifties kitchen stuff, actually mid century stuff in general...so much fun to photograph!</td>', 'Originally posted by Napalm Nymph: What an awesome idea!  (I happen to love old horror movies).  You''ve executed it so well...the shadows on the wall are perfect.  How did you aquire that mixer?  My best friend has a stove in her kitchen from 1951...it''s baby blue and oh so fun.  You''ve just reminded me that I must photograph it.   The mixer was my father-in-laws, he, I think, "liberated" it from a closed down diner in Philly...so the story goes. I just LOVE fifties kitchen stuff, actually mid century stuff in general...so much fun to photograph!', '2005-09-20 15:28:33.000000', NULL, 0),
